2. Reduce manual administrative work.
3. Simplify citizen-government interactions.
4. Provide intelligent government service discovery.
5. Improve application processing and tracking.
6. Automate document processing and verification assistance.
7. Enable predictive analytics for government departments.
8. Detect unusual patterns and potential fraud indicators.
9. Improve public transparency and accountability.
10. Support Tamil and English communication.
11. Provide data-driven decision support.
12. Build an extensible digital governance ecosystem.

